# The stand the dev proxy forwards /crm/* to. Copy this file to .env and set your own.
# An environment variable of the same name overrides the file.
#
# Mind that the distribution of the stand has to match platformName in
# src/environments/environment.development.ts: that one is compiled into the bundle and
# does not follow this address on its own. A Creatio stand with the BPMSoft name set (or
# the other way round) sends batch queries with a foreign __type contract.
#
CRM_BACKEND=http://localhost:80

# The workspace prefix the dev proxy puts in front of routes with scope "workspace".
# Empty by default: an application on .NET Core does not use one, and a prefix added for nothing
# makes the requests fail. Routes with scope "application" never get it on any stand.
#
# What to put here is reported by the platform itself. Open a platform page and look at
# workspaceBaseUrl in its global:
#
#   http://localhost:80/0   carries the number -> CRM_WORKSPACE=/0
#   http://localhost:80     carries none       -> leave empty
#
# In embedded mode that address comes from the platform, here this variable stands in for it.
#CRM_WORKSPACE=/0
